          <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-60210" fontColor="#000000" lineColor="#000000" textAlignment="1">
            <bounds x="720" y="348" width="354" height="109"/>
            <content>Based on ISA-95 Part 1 Figure 3, Page 19, Figure 4, page 23. This view applies the ArchiMate definition of location &quot;A location is defined as a conceptual point or extent in space.&quot; to machinery as well, since machinery occupies space. All machinery is assumed also to have a processing capacity, i.e. a node that can run control applications, including ones that are embedded.</content>
          </child>
