          <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-a15da36b5fa64e6ca02e6cce0853cf07" textAlignment="1">
            <bounds x="28" y="372" width="862" height="110"/>
            <content>ISA-95 has broad industry support. It is managed by the International Society for Automation, which is a professional organization that claims over 30,000 members. ISA-95 is supported in products from major IT suppliers, such as IBM, SAP, and Oracle, and is also the basis for IEC 62241 (Nuclear Power Plants – Main Control Room – Alarm Functions and Presentation). https://www.isa.org/standards-and-publications/isa-standards/isa-95-standard&#xD;
&#xD;
The Business to Manufacturing Markup Language (B2MML V0700 MESA International) implements ISA-95 in XML, and is also the basis for IEC 62264 (Enterprise-Control System Integration). https://mesa.org/topics-resources/b2mml/</content>
          </child>
          <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-213fcf5e1574430ba2226d51c6310d26" textAlignment="1" imagePath="images/__y9JAGR7EfG_Vq-miMQlHg.png" imagePosition="4">
            <bounds x="28" y="492" width="721" height="445"/>
          </child>
